      "extract": "We first cite some concepts and results from the literature [@Sh; @b72; @b76] which are related to Gröbner-Shirshov bases for associative algebras. A notion of the pre-Gröbner-Shirshov basis is new. Let $X$ be a set and $F$ a field, $F\\langle X\\rangle$ the free associative algebra over $F$ generated by $X$, and $X^*$ the free monoid generated by $X$. A well ordering $<$ on $X^*$ is monomial if for any $u, v\\in X^*$,",
