      "extract": "Let $\\Sigma=\\{\\sigma_1, \\cdots, \\sigma_n\\}$ be a finite set. Let $M=(m_{ij})$ be a symmetric $n\\times n$ matrix over the natural numbers together with $\\infty$, such that $m_{ii}=1,\\ 2\\leq m_{ij}\\leq\\infty$ for $i\\neq j$. Such an M is called a Coxeter matrix. Now, we use $W$ to denote $$W=W(M)=sgp\\langle \\Sigma|(\\sigma_i\\sigma_j)^{m_{ij}}=1,\\ 1\\leq i,\\ j\\leq n,\\ m_{ij}\\neq\\infty\\rangle.$$ W is called the Coxeter",
